# Civic AI Club — how we work in this repo

This repository is **standalone and public**: `CivicAIClub/ext-a-green-valley-hospitality`. It is an **external client** engagement with a local business, so the club's reputation depends on how carefully we handle their information. All paths are relative to the repo root.

The developers are high school students learning collaborative coding. Prefer clarity over cleverness. If you generate code the developer cannot explain, say so and summarize what it does in plain English.

## Client data (non-negotiable)

- **Never commit client data. Sales PDFs, exports, spreadsheets, customer lists, and email lists stay in a gitignored data/ folder or in Drive, never in git.**
- `.gitignore` blocks `data/*` (except `data/README.md`), `*.pdf`, `*.xlsx`, `*.xls`, `*.xlsm`, and `*.csv`. Never suggest `git add -f` to get around it.
- No personal contact details beyond what is already in `README.md`: no phone numbers, customer names, or email addresses in code, comments, tests, commit messages, or PR descriptions.
- Tests and examples use fabricated values, labeled as fake.
- If you notice client data staged or committed, stop and tell the developer to contact Cayden. Deleting it in a later commit does not remove it from history.

## Git rules (non-negotiable)

- **Never push to `main`.** Always work on a branch and open a pull request. Merging requires one approving review.
- **Branch names:** `feature/<short-description>`, `fix/<short-description>`, or `chore/<short-description>`. Lowercase, hyphens, no spaces.
- **Never commit secrets.** No API keys, tokens, mailbox passwords, or `.env` files. Every environment variable gets a placeholder line in `.env.example`.
- Small, frequent commits with plain-English messages.
- Pull requests use the template in `.github/pull_request_template.md`.

## Talking to the client

- In anything the client will see (emails, demos, docs you hand over), describe the work as a time-saving tool. Don't lead with "AI", and don't name the school's faculty projects.
- Don't promise scope or timelines without Cayden.

## Where things live

- Beginner Git walkthrough, common fixes, and the club-wide repository list: **https://github.com/CivicAIClub/docs/blob/main/developer-onboarding.md**. Reference it for any Git, branching, PR, or merge-conflict question instead of improvising.
- Project context for this repo: `README.md` and `.cursor/rules/ext-a-green-valley-hospitality.mdc`.
